  "title": "Floodstone Builders",
  "rules": [
    "Three miners share two picks, one wrench and five initial stones. Turn toward a block or worker to interact.",
    "Mine with a pick: the block vanishes, opening both walking space and possible water connectivity.",
    "One stone builds a support or floodwall. A two-stone pump needs a neighboring support and the wrench.",
    "Work the supported pump to drain nearby cells for this tick. A wall blocks water and miners.",
    "Water spreads one cardinal cell every third tick from existing flooded floor; the spring stays wet.",
    "Wet miners lose breath. Zero breath requires a front-facing rescue that spends one stone.",
    "A forward stone pass changes a teammate inventory immediately. Tools circulate through the camp cache.",
    "Bank all ore at camp. Every banked unit pays the team; the depositor privately prefers one ore vein.",
    "The scene uses original block stone, timber posts, metal hand pumps, miner packs and visible water; every flood overlay binds actual water cells."
  ],
